delta-change "source-provenance"
message "SourceProvenance: lossless source provenance"
author "ai"
doc "guide" """
  |# SourceProvenance: lossless source provenance
  |
  |SourceProvenance is the first source-preserving layer above LexicalCodecs. It is a product
  |slice, not a new bootstrap foundation. F0-F11 remain frozen.
  |
  |## Identity
  |
  |- predecessor: LexicalCodecs
  |- delta: `256ca4fb85cace93ff2580cb0837be48ad40564751e178f4eba0bc33b56b6196`
  |- root: `3e84ee39aa514ff2ff96dd27c35e6a8c6df3b4619d34fb24a926de4d810287fb`
  |- graph size: 473 nodes, 624 edges, 473 entities
  |
  |## Purpose
  |
  |LexicalCodecs separates token recognition from semantic lexical values. SourceProvenance
  |adds a second, orthogonal result: exact lexical provenance. Semantic parsing
  |still normalizes programs, while `lexSource` preserves the original source.
  |
  |A source document records:
  |
  |- raw token source text,
  |- a half-open UTF-8 byte span for each token,
  |- leading trivia for each token,
  |- trailing trivia after the last token,
  |- decoded lexical values separately through the LexicalCodecs codec layer.
  |
  |Whitespace and `//` line comments are trivia. They are not injected into the
  |semantic AST and therefore cannot perturb program meaning.
  |
  |## Graph-resident source policy
  |
  |`source.bool0.policy` selects first-class values for:
  |
  |- offset unit: `utf8-bytes`,
  |- trivia mode: `preserve`,
  |- attachment: `leading`,
  |- reconstruction: `exact`.
  |
  |The policy is connected to `grammar.bool0` through `grammar.source`. SourceProvenance
  |also introduces `source7.schema` and source vocabulary components for document,
  |token, span, trivia, policy, offset unit, trivia mode, attachment, and
  |reconstruction.
  |
  |The semantic law is:
  |
  |```text
  |lexSource(source).renderLossless == source
  |```
  |
  |while normalized printing remains:
  |
  |```text
  |print(parse(source)) == canonical surface text
  |```
  |
  |These are intentionally different views of the same program.
  |
  |## UTF-8 coordinates
  |
  |Spans use UTF-8 byte offsets rather than JVM UTF-16 indices. For example:
  |
  |```text
  |π&&true
  |```
  |
  |has token spans:
  |
  |```text
  |π     [0,2)
  |&&    [2,4)
  |true  [4,8)
  |```
  |
  |This coordinate system is portable across Scala, Rust, editors, repositories,
  |and future binary/source adapters.
  |
  |## Free changes
  |
  |`DeltaBool0` is extended to admit source-policy entities. Edits remain
  |fail-closed. Disabling whitespace preservation, changing the reconstruction
  |contract away from `exact`, or selecting an unsupported coordinate unit makes
  |the graph invalid.
  |
  |Language-owned nodes may retain typed links to shared schema/component nodes
  |when they are rewritten; this does not grant permission to mutate the shared
  |schema itself.
  |
  |## Deliberate boundary
  |
  |SourceProvenance preserves lexical provenance but does not yet assign spans to every AST
  |node and does not synthesize INDENT/DEDENT layout tokens. Those can be layered
  |next using this lossless token/trivia substrate rather than rediscovering source
  |positions later.
  |
  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "lexical-codecs"
  assert "introduces" "grammar.component.source" "grammar.component"
